
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:setname@

%9Parameters:%9

    The new real name.

%9Description:%9

    Changes your real name (the 'gecos' shown in WHOIS) on the active server
    without reconnecting. The name is sent with the SETNAME command, which
    only servers with the IRCv3 'setname' capability understand; erssi
    requests that capability when it connects, but sends the command in any
    case. Such servers pass the change on to the clients that share a
    channel with you and support the capability.

    Only the current connection is changed; to keep the new name for later
    connections, change the real_name setting or the -realname of the
    network.

%9Examples:%9

    /SETNAME Alice Example
    /SETNAME Away from keyboard

%9See also:%9 NETWORK, SET, WHOIS

